      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Marshall,_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town became the county seat of Saline County in 1839, replacing Jefferson, and its courthouse built in 1882 now sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        17,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/Marshall,_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Missouri Valley College, founded in 1889 after a 1874 conference in Sarcoxie, has its original Baity Hall listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
